NAME
    log - emit one localized structured runtime log record

SYNOPSIS
    log <severity> <domain> <message-id> [<field> <value>]...

DESCRIPTION
    log emits a structured record to standard error when the requested severity
    is enabled by m_LOG_LEVEL.

    Supported severities are:
        fatal error warn info debug trace

    Message text is resolved through the technical lang facility. Additional
    fields are supplied as name/value pairs and are appended to the record.

    m_LOG_LEVEL accepts the current filtering levels off/none, fatal, error,
    warn, info, debug and trace/all.

ENVIRONMENT
    Requires a nonempty m_ROOT inherited from an initialized m environment.
    From an uninitialized host shell, invoke m log [arguments].


EXIT STATUS
    0   The invocation was valid, whether the record was emitted or filtered.
    Non-zero status indicates invalid severity, log level, identifiers or field
        arguments.

SEE ALSO
    lang
